rewritten:
arf! it's hello world time again! ^^

1) using cout:

```cpp
#include <iostream>

int main() {
    std::cout << "Hello world!" << std::endl;
    return 0;
}
```

2) using printf:

```cpp
#include <stdio.h>

int main() {
    printf("Hello world!\n");
    return 0;
}
```

3) using puts:

```cpp
#include <stdio.h>

int main() {
    puts("Hello world!");
    return 0;
}
```

4) using stringstream:

```cpp
#include <iostream>
#include <sstream>

int main() {
    std::stringstream ss;
    ss << "Hello world!";
    std::cout << ss.str() << std::endl;
    return 0;
}
```

5) using write():

```cpp
#include <unistd.h>
#include <string.h>

int main() {
    const char* s = "Hello world!\n";
    write(STDOUT_FILENO, s, strlen(s));
    return 0;
}
```

and that's five different ways to say hello! each one has its own use case, but they all print the same thing to the console, wan~
